    <summary>Syncs the listening port of qBittorrent, Transmission, Deluge, or Nicotine+ with the VPN-assigned port, and imports media files into Plex-compatible library folders</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
## qbPortWeaver

A lightweight Windows system tray application that keeps the listening port of **qBittorrent**, **Transmission**, **Deluge**, or **Nicotine+** in sync with the port assigned by your VPN.

### VPN Support

Works with **ProtonVPN** (log file or NAT-PMP), **PIA** (`piactl`), and any **NAT-PMP capable VPN or router** (RFC 6886). ProtonVPN's earlier protocols and the newer Proton Protocols (Proton WireGuard, Proton Stealth) are both detected automatically. The provider is selectable from Settings.

### Port Sync

Updates the client's listening port via its API on a configurable interval whenever the VPN-assigned port changes. Can restart or force-start the client, apply a fallback port when the VPN is disconnected, and verify the port is reachable from the Internet with optional automatic recovery. At startup it waits briefly for the VPN to finish connecting before reporting it as disconnected.

### Media Manager

Imports movie and TV episode files into Plex-compatible library folders on each cycle, using The Movie Database (TMDB) for naming via hardlink, copy, or move. Preview before applying, with uncertain matches highlighted for review. A free TMDB API key is required.

### Other Features

- Status panel and color-coded tray icon showing the live sync state, with a persisted history of recent port changes, session statistics, an on-demand port reachability test, and an auto-recovery line showing failures building toward a recovery attempt or the wait until the next one
- One-click diagnostics that health-check the whole sync chain and suggest fixes
- In-app update that downloads and installs new versions, plus an automatic update checker
- Built-in user guide with a browsable contents tree and search, available offline from the tray menu
- Built-in log viewer with levels, live tail, search, filters, and rotated backup browsing; tray alerts on warnings or errors
- Consistent light and dark theming across every window and pop-up dialog, following your chosen Windows color mode
- Interface mismatch warning when qBittorrent or Nicotine+ is not bound to the VPN adapter, plus automatic repair when qBittorrent's stored adapter binding stops resolving after a VPN reconnect
- Auto-Recovery that restarts VPN services or cycles the adapter after failures persist
- Sync on network change, pause/resume from the tray, connection test and client auto-detect in Settings
- Post-update command hook, JSON status file, and optional auto-start with Windows

For full setup instructions, see https://github.com/martsg666/qbPortWeaver#readme
    ]]></description>
